  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Polio Eradication Phase IV Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to contribute to the improvement of health and wellbeing of Pakistani children through eradication of Polio. The specific objective of the project is to permanently interrupt WPV1 circulation and all types of polioviruses, including cVPDV2, by the end of 2023, and maintain &#x2018;Polio Free&#x2019; status for subsequent three years. To this end, the project will support countrywide mass Polio vaccination campaigns targeting more than 41 million children below five years of age, along with undertaking extensive community sensitization/mobilization as well as high standard surveillance activities for PEP</narrative>
  </description>
